00:08:59.450 --> 00:09:01.830
"Gina and Ayaka's
Hand Grip Training Lesson"

00:09:01.870 --> 00:09:06.620
Now we'll explain how to
work out with a hand grip!

00:09:06.620 --> 00:09:09.950
Lots of guys are in love
with beefy forearms!

00:09:09.950 --> 00:09:14.870
As for women, a powerful grip will help
make your everyday life more pleasant!

00:09:14.870 --> 00:09:19.700
You can buy handgrips at sporting-goods
and home improvement stores.

00:09:19.700 --> 00:09:26.000
The amount of resistance varies, so a
low-level one won't give you a workout.

00:09:26.000 --> 00:09:31.620
Conversely, you should avoid high-level
ones that you can't close even once.

00:09:31.620 --> 00:09:36.120
On that topic, here's the average grip
strength of Japanese 20-somethings.

00:09:36.120 --> 00:09:38.750
It's around 46 kg for men,

00:09:38.750 --> 00:09:41.830
and 28 kg for women.

00:09:41.830 --> 00:09:43.200
We recommend starting with a resistance
you can close for a set of 10 to 15 reps.

00:09:43.200 --> 00:09:47.910
"10~15 Reps"
We recommend starting with a resistance
you can close for a set of 10 to 15 reps.

00:09:47.910 --> 00:09:52.200
"10~15 Reps"
That kind of resistance is good
for using up any surplus energy.

00:09:52.200 --> 00:09:54.370
Using a hand grip is very simple.

00:09:54.370 --> 00:09:59.290
Slowly close and release
the gripper without cheating.

00:09:59.290 --> 00:10:01.410
That's the basic workout.

00:10:01.410 --> 00:10:04.750
Try 3 sets of 15 to 20 reps.

00:10:04.750 --> 00:10:08.870
One form of applied training involves
using a grip you can't close with one hand

00:10:08.870 --> 00:10:15.200
by forcing it closed with both hands
and opening it as slowly as possible.

00:10:15.200 --> 00:10:18.290
Of course, this ups
the resistance substantially.

00:10:18.290 --> 00:10:22.040
Hand grips train your forearm muscles.

00:10:22.040 --> 00:10:25.330
Training them will also improve your grip.

00:10:25.330 --> 00:10:29.370
A better grip will increase your
strength training performance overall,

00:10:29.370 --> 00:10:34.250
and it's surprisingly helpful
in many everyday situations.

00:10:34.250 --> 00:10:39.080
If you train regularly, you might have
that strength when you need it!

00:10:39.080 --> 00:10:43.750
Use the hand grip correctly,
and strive to improve your grip strength!

00:10:48.250 --> 00:10:52.620
That gripper boasts the third
strongest resistance in the world.

00:10:52.620 --> 00:10:57.250
Only about a hundred people
worldwide can close it with one hand.

